    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter the July 25th slate with a highly optimized lineup, anchored by the elite daily efficiency of **Junior Caminero** (71.46) and **Colt Keith** (69.64). **Junior Caminero** remains a priority start against Tanner Bibee, as his strong xwOBA of 0.376 provides the highest floor on the roster despite a neutral park environment. Meanwhile, **Colt Keith** benefits from a prime leadoff spot and a favorable platoon matchup against Michael Wacha, with his score bolstered significantly by a +9% boost from the pitcher's efficiency profile. In the outfield, **Christian Yelich** (74.33) is our strongest overall play of the day; his +13% platoon boost against Dakota Feltner, combined with the leadoff role, positions him to lead our offensive output as we prioritize aggressive SB and R potential.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench today involves **Lars Nootbaar**, who fell just shy of a start with a 43.93 score. While his platoon advantage against Hunter Greene typically warrants consideration, the opposing pitcher\u2019s elite skill profile (-19% impact) and the ambiguity of the \"Lineup Pending\" status made him a risky pivot compared to the guaranteed leadoff duties of **Pete Crow-Armstrong**. Although **Pete Crow-Armstrong** faces the daunting challenge of Paul Skenes, his +14% platoon edge and the imperative to hunt for stolen bases\u2014our scarcest category\u2014keep him in the lineup. We are also closely monitoring the statuses of **Yordan Alvarez** and **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, both of whom are currently projected based on assumed lineup spots; should either drop down the order, their efficiency scores will likely regress, necessitating a potential shift toward the more stable, albeit lower-ceiling, options like **Carson Benge** currently sitting on the bench.",
